To place a clickable SVG icon (like a magnifying glass) to the **right side** of an input field and have it trigger a function on click, you can use HTML and CSS to position the icon and JavaScript to handle the click event.

Here’s a minimal and clean example:

---

### ✅ HTML + CSS + JavaScript Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Search Input with Icon</title>
  <style>
    .search-container {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
    }

    .search-input {
      padding-right: 30px; /* Make space for the icon */
    }

    .search-icon {
      position: absolute;
      right: 5px;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      cursor: pointer;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="search-container">
    <input type="text" class="search-input" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search...">
    <svg class="search-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <path d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
    </svg>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.querySelector('.search-icon').addEventListener('click', function () {
      const query = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
      console.log('Search query:', query);
      // Call your function here
      performSearch(query);
    });

    function performSearch(query) {
      // Your search logic here
      alert('Searching for: ' + query);
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🔍 Explanation

- **`.search-container`**: A wrapper to hold the input and the icon.
- **`.search-input`**: The input field with padding to avoid text overlapping the icon.
- **`.search-icon`**: The SVG icon absolutely positioned to the right of the input.
- **JavaScript**: Listens for a click on the icon and retrieves the input value to pass to a function.

